 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Booking Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a booking form?\", \"a\": \"A booking form is how a customer claims a time or a resource you have a limited supply of. It records the request and the slot they want. A good one offers only times that are still open and turns each request into a confirmed booking.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a booking form?\", \"a\": \"Describe the booking in plain English to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, including how long a slot runs and any check before someone books. You get the form, the rules that hide taken times and a table where every booking is stored. Change any rule later by asking.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to write a reservation form?\", \"a\": \"Start with the fields that confirm the reservation: name, phone or email, date, time and party size or quantity. Add only questions you will act on, like dietary needs for a table. A reservation form should also say plainly how to cancel and by when.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does a booking form look like?\", \"a\": \"Most booking forms fit on one phone screen. The customer picks a service, then a calendar opens on the first free day with a row of times beneath it. Name and email follow, then a deposit step if you charge one. The last screen repeats the date and time back so the customer can check it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a reservation form the same as a booking form?\", \"a\": \"Mostly, yes. Both set something aside for a named person on a chosen day. A reservation form counts down a fixed stock of seats or rooms until none are left. An appointment form treats each hour of one person's time as a single slot that vanishes once taken.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a booking form template include?\", \"a\": \"A booking form template needs the person's name and contact details, the service or resource they want, and the date and time. Add a deposit step if no-shows cost you money. Include a field for anything you must prepare before they arrive.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does an online booking form work?\", \"a\": \"An online booking form checks your calendar whenever someone opens it and lists only the slots nobody holds yet. On submit, the slot is held, the booking is saved as a row, and a confirmation email goes out. A form on paper cannot run that check before a customer picks.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where can I find a booking form template?\", \"a\": \"Form builders and template galleries carry booking form templates for salons, rentals, and classes, and most cost nothing to copy. A template supplies the fields but not the calendar behind them. Opening hours and slot length are still yours to set. Emergent starts the form from your own booking rules instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a free booking form?\", \"a\": \"Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing a booking form. When the money matters more than the time slot, such as a fee with no appointment attached, a payment form is the better fit.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is there a booking form app?\", \"a\": \"Emergent builds the booking form as a web app that customers open in a phone browser. A custom domain is included and paid for in credits. Staff use the same app to see the day's bookings. For clients who need to share history first, pair it with an intake form.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
